IMPORT prelude

-- Society of Saint Maur Incorporation Ordinance 1923 (Singapore) -- who the corporation sole is and when a successor Lady Superior
-- qualifies (ss 2, 3), Gazette evidence of her appointment (s 4), when a deed is duly sealed (s 5(2)), the Corporation's powers to sue
-- and to deal in property (s 5(1), (3), (4)), the 2024 change of name (s 7) and the saving of other persons' rights (s 8).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation -- "version in force from 25/3/2024" -- as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SSMIO1923.txt. The latest
-- amendment annotated is Act 7 of 2024 (Society of Saint Maur Incorporation (Amendment) Act 2024), wef 25 March 2024, which rewrote
-- ss 2-5, repealed s 6, added s 7 and deleted the three Schedules. The body's section numbers are followed; the arrangement at the top
-- of the deposit lists the headings one line out of step with their numbers.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0251 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. For a person or business the Ordinance decides three things: whether the woman claiming to act as the
-- Corporation is qualified to, whether a deed the Corporation executes is duly sealed, and what name it must be sued or contracted
-- with under. The whole operative text is encoded.
-- Not encoded: the preamble (the history of the three Convents of the Holy Infant Jesus and the repealed Penang Ordinance No. 192),
-- s 1 (short title), the repealed s 6 and the deleted Schedules, and anything in s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886
-- beyond whether a power of attorney was deposited under it.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions (as followed in the example rows). No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Society of Saint Maur Incorporation Ordinance 1923 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2 and 3 -- the corporation sole and a qualified successor`

-- s 2: "The said Euphrasie Labordenave and her successors for the time being in the office of Lady Superior in Penang of the Society
-- of Saint Maur appointed for Singapore and duly qualified as hereinafter provided shall be a body corporate (hereinafter called "the
-- Corporation"), and shall have perpetual succession under the name of "The Lady Superior of the Convent of the Holy Infant Jesus"."
-- s 3: "No successor ... shall be deemed to be qualified as such successor unless and until her appointment as such Lady Superior has
-- been notified to the Minister, and the same has been approved by him, and unless and until a notification of such approval has
-- appeared in the Gazette."
-- The three conditions in s 3 are cumulative ("and ... and unless and until"). s 3 speaks only of a "successor"; the named first holder
-- needs none of them.
DECLARE Holder HAS
    `is Euphrasie Labordenave` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointed Lady Superior in Penang of the Society for Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointment notified to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointment approved by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approval notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the successor is qualified under section 3` IF
        `the holder`'s `appointed Lady Superior in Penang of the Society for Singapore`
    AND `the holder`'s `appointment notified to the Minister`
    AND `the holder`'s `appointment approved by the Minister`
    AND `the holder`'s `approval notified in the Gazette`

GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holder is the Corporation` IF
        `the holder`'s `is Euphrasie Labordenave`
    OR  `the successor is qualified under section 3` `the holder`

§§ `4 -- the Gazette as evidence`

-- s 4: "A notification in the Gazette of the approval of an appointment of a person as Lady Superior ... for Singapore shall be
-- sufficient evidence that such person was duly appointed as such Lady Superior and is duly qualified as by this Ordinance is required."
-- The Gazette notice alone is enough evidence of BOTH the appointment and every s 3 condition. "Sufficient" evidence is not said to be
-- conclusive; whether it can be rebutted is not decided here (inference not drawn).
GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Gazette notice is sufficient evidence of qualification` IF
    `the holder`'s `approval notified in the Gazette`

§§ `5(2) -- a duly sealed instrument`

-- s 5(2): instruments "shall be deemed to be duly sealed if such seal be affixed in the presence of the said Euphrasie Labordenave or
-- other the Lady Superior ... appointed for Singapore for the time being, or by her attorney duly authorised by a Power of Attorney
-- deposited under section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, and if each such deed, document or other instrument be
-- signed by the said Euphrasie Labordenave or her successor for Singapore or her attorney so authorised as aforesaid, and such signing
-- shall be and be taken as sufficient evidence that the seal of the Corporation was duly and properly affixed, and that the same is
-- the lawful seal of the Corporation."
-- Two limbs, both needed: (i) affixing -- in the Lady Superior's presence, or by a deposited attorney; (ii) signing -- by the Lady
-- Superior or by an attorney "so authorised" (that is, by a deposited power). An attorney whose power was never deposited satisfies
-- neither limb.
DECLARE Sealing HAS
    `seal affixed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `affixed in the presence of the Lady Superior` IS A BOOLEAN
    `affixed by her attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the Lady Superior` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by her attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
    `power of attorney deposited under section 48` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the sealing` IS A Sealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the attorney is duly authorised` IF
    `the sealing`'s `power of attorney deposited under section 48`

GIVEN `the sealing` IS A Sealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seal was properly affixed` IF
        `the sealing`'s `seal affixed`
    AND (    `the sealing`'s `affixed in the presence of the Lady Superior`
         OR (`the sealing`'s `affixed by her attorney` AND `the attorney is duly authorised` `the sealing`))

GIVEN `the sealing` IS A Sealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument was properly signed` IF
        `the sealing`'s `signed by the Lady Superior`
    OR (`the sealing`'s `signed by her attorney` AND `the attorney is duly authorised` `the sealing`)

GIVEN `the sealing` IS A Sealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is deemed duly sealed` IF
        `the seal was properly affixed` `the sealing`
    AND `the instrument was properly signed` `the sealing`

-- "such signing shall be and be taken as sufficient evidence that the seal ... was duly and properly affixed": a proper signature is
-- itself the evidence of proper affixing.
GIVEN `the sealing` IS A Sealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence of due sealing` IF
    `the instrument was properly signed` `the sealing`

§§ `5(1), (3) and (4) -- what the Corporation may do`

-- s 5(1): "may have and use a corporate seal which may from time to time be broken, changed, altered and made anew as to the
-- Corporation seems fit." s 5(3): "may sue and be sued in respect of its property or otherwise in all Courts of Justice." s 5(4): "may
-- acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description, and may sell, exchange, convey, assign,
-- surrender and yield up, mortgage, demise, re-assign, transfer or otherwise dispose of" it "upon such terms as to the Corporation
-- shall seem fit."
-- No provision of the Ordinance makes any of these subject to the Minister's approval; only the Lady Superior's appointment is (s 3).
-- The last two acts below are not conferred by THIS Ordinance; whether the Corporation has them by other law is not decided here.
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `change its seal`
    `sue in any court`
    `be sued in any court`
    `buy land`
    `hold movable property`
    `sell land`
    `mortgage land`
    `lease land`
    `carry on a business for profit`
    `borrow money without security`

GIVEN `the act` IS AN Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance gives the Corporation the power` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `carry on a business for profit` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `borrow money without security` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the act` IS AN Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance requires the Minister's approval for the act` IF
    FALSE

§§ `2 and 7 -- the name, and the 2024 change of name`

-- s 7(1): "As from the date of publication in the Gazette of the Society of Saint Maur Incorporation (Amendment) Act 2024, any reference
-- in any written law or document to the Corporation by the name "The Lady Superior of the Convent of the Holy Infant Jesus in Penang" is
-- to be read as a reference to the Corporation by the name "The Lady Superior of the Convent of the Holy Infant Jesus"."
-- s 7(2): the change "does not affect the identity of the Corporation or any rights or obligations of the Corporation or render
-- defective any legal proceedings by or against the Corporation, and any legal proceedings that might have been continued or commenced
-- by or against it by its former name may be continued or commenced by or against it by its new name."
-- The date of Gazette publication of the 2024 Act is not in the deposit; the annotations give its commencement as 25 March 2024. The
-- encoding takes "after publication" as a fact.
DECLARE Name IS ONE OF
    `The Lady Superior of the Convent of the Holy Infant Jesus in Penang`
    `The Lady Superior of the Convent of the Holy Infant Jesus`

GIVEN `after publication of the 2024 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Name
`the Corporation's name` MEANS
    IF `after publication of the 2024 Act`
    THEN `The Lady Superior of the Convent of the Holy Infant Jesus`
    ELSE `The Lady Superior of the Convent of the Holy Infant Jesus in Penang`

GIVEN `the name used` IS A Name, `after publication of the 2024 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Name
`a reference in a written law or document is read as` MEANS
    IF `after publication of the 2024 Act`
    THEN `The Lady Superior of the Convent of the Holy Infant Jesus`
    ELSE `the name used`

GIVEN `begun under the former name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceedings are rendered defective by the change of name` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `could have been brought under the former name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceedings may be brought under the new name` IF
    `could have been brought under the former name`

§§ `8 -- saving of Government and other rights`

-- s 8: "Nothing in this Ordinance shall affect the rights of the Government or of any body politic or corporate or of any other persons
-- except such as are mentioned in this Ordinance and those claiming by, through, from or under them."
-- A person's rights are open to the Ordinance only if she is a person mentioned in it (the Society, the Lady Superior, the Corporation)
-- or claims by, through, from or under one. The Minister is mentioned (s 3); whether that brings the Government within the exception is
-- not decided here, and a fixture for the Government is set as NOT mentioned (inference).
GIVEN `is mentioned in the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims through a person mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect the person's rights` IF
    `is mentioned in the Ordinance` OR `claims through a person mentioned`
